-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore), 2020 RE, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.
-- LAYER 1, PART 5: RIGHTS OF UNPAID SELLER AGAINST THE GOODS (ss 38 to 48).
-- These are the unpaid seller's rights; the buyer meets them as what the seller may do to the buyer's goods.
-- Section 40 is "[Omitted in 1994 Revised Edition]": nothing to encode (coverage row s 40).
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the text gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer on
-- these facts".  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`

DECLARE `Method of exercising the right of stoppage` IS ONE OF
    `taking actual possession of the goods`
    `giving notice of his claim to the carrier or other bailee or custodier in whose possession the goods are`
    `some other method`

DECLARE `Person to whom notice of stoppage is given` IS ONE OF
    `the person in actual possession of the goods`
    `the principal of the person in actual possession of the goods`
    `some other person`

DECLARE `Disposition of a document of title by the buyer` IS ONE OF
    `a sale by the transferee`
    `a pledge or other disposition for value`
    `some other transfer`

§ `Part 5 -- Rights of unpaid seller against the goods`

§§ `Preliminary (ss 38 and 39)`

-- s 38(1).
-- src:1116 | 38.—(1) The seller of goods is an unpaid seller within the meaning
-- src:1117 | of this Act —
-- src:1119 | (a) when the whole of the price has not been paid or tendered;
-- src:1121 | (b) when a bill of exchange or other negotiable instrument has
-- src:1122 | been received as conditional payment, and the condition on
-- src:1123 | which it was received has not been fulfilled by reason of
-- src:1124 | the dishonour of the instrument or otherwise.
@ref s 38(1) (src:1116-1124)
GIVEN `the whole of the price has not been paid or tendered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a bill of exchange or other negotiable instrument has been received as conditional payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition on which it was received has not been fulfilled by reason of the dishonour of the instrument or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 38(1) the seller of goods is an unpaid seller` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the whole of the price has not been paid or tendered`
          OR (`a bill of exchange or other negotiable instrument has been received as conditional payment` AND `the condition on which it was received has not been fulfilled by reason of the dishonour of the instrument or otherwise`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The seller of goods is an unpaid seller within the meaning of this Act (a) when the whole of the price has not been paid or tendered; (b) when a bill of exchange or other negotiable instrument has been received as conditional payment, and the condition on which it was received has not been fulfilled"
            -- MARGINAL (a): the two "when" cases are read as the definition of "unpaid seller" within the meaning of the Act, so a seller in neither case is not an unpaid seller; the other reading is that "when" limits the grant and the text is silent about other sellers.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 38(2).
-- src:1126 | (2) In this Part, “seller” includes any person who is in the position
-- src:1127 | of a seller, as, for instance, an agent of the seller to whom the bill of
-- src:1128 | lading has been indorsed, or a consignor or agent who has himself
-- src:1129 | paid (or is directly responsible for) the price.
@ref s 38(2) (src:1126-1129)
GIVEN `the person is in the position of a seller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 38(2) the person is a seller for the purposes of Part 5` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is in the position of a seller`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In this Part, “seller” includes any person who is in the position of a seller, as, for instance, an agent of the seller to whom the bill of lading has been indorsed, or a consignor or agent who has himself paid (or is directly responsible for) the price" -- the list is not closed.
            NOTHING

-- s 39(1)(a).
-- src:1132 | 39.—(1) Subject to this and any other Act, notwithstanding that the
-- src:1134 | property in the goods may have passed to the buyer, the unpaid seller
-- src:1135 | of goods, as such, has by implication of law —
-- src:1140 | (a) a lien on the goods or right to retain them for the price
-- src:1141 | while he is in possession of them;
@ref s 39(1)(a) (src:1132-1141)
GIVEN `the seller is an unpaid seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller is in possession of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Act takes the right away` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39(1)(a) the unpaid seller has by implication of law a lien on the goods or right to retain them for the price` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `another Act takes the right away`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to this and any other Act", and another Act is not among the sources.
            NOTHING
        IF `the seller is an unpaid seller` AND `the seller is in possession of the goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the lien is given "to the unpaid seller" "while he is in possession of them". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (wh): "while" read as "where" (assumed, not ruled; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 39(1)(b).
-- src:1132 | 39.—(1) Subject to this and any other Act, notwithstanding that the
-- src:1134 | property in the goods may have passed to the buyer, the unpaid seller
-- src:1135 | of goods, as such, has by implication of law —
-- src:1140 | (a) a lien on the goods or right to retain them for the price
-- src:1141 | while he is in possession of them;
-- src:1143 | (b) in case of the insolvency of the buyer, a right of stopping
-- src:1144 | the goods in transit after he has parted with the possession
-- src:1145 | of them;
@ref s 39(1)(b) (src:1132-1145)
GIVEN `the seller is an unpaid seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer is insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller has parted with the possession of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Act takes the right away` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39(1)(b) the unpaid seller has by implication of law a right of stopping the goods in transit` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `another Act takes the right away`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to this and any other Act", and another Act is not among the sources.
            NOTHING
        IF `the seller is an unpaid seller` AND `the buyer is insolvent` AND `the seller has parted with the possession of the goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the right is given "in case of the insolvency of the buyer, ... after he has parted with the possession of them". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (k): "in the case of" read as "where" (assumed, not ruled; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 39(1)(c).
-- src:1132 | 39.—(1) Subject to this and any other Act, notwithstanding that the
-- src:1134 | property in the goods may have passed to the buyer, the unpaid seller
-- src:1135 | of goods, as such, has by implication of law —
-- src:1140 | (a) a lien on the goods or right to retain them for the price
-- src:1141 | while he is in possession of them;
-- src:1143 | (b) in case of the insolvency of the buyer, a right of stopping
-- src:1144 | the goods in transit after he has parted with the possession
-- src:1145 | of them;
-- src:1147 | (c) a right of re-sale as limited by this Act.
@ref s 39(1)(c) (src:1132-1147)
GIVEN `the seller is an unpaid seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Act takes the right away` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39(1)(c) the unpaid seller has by implication of law a right of re-sale as limited by this Act` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `another Act takes the right away`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to this and any other Act", and another Act is not among the sources.
            NOTHING
        IF `the seller is an unpaid seller` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is given to "the unpaid seller of goods, as such".
            NOTHING

-- s 39(2).
-- src:1149 | (2) Where the property in goods has not passed to the buyer, the
-- src:1150 | unpaid seller has (in addition to his other remedies) a right of
-- src:1151 | withholding delivery similar to and co-extensive with his rights of
-- src:1152 | lien or retention and stoppage in transit where the property has passed
-- src:1153 | to the buyer.
@ref s 39(2) (src:1149-1153)
GIVEN `the seller is an unpaid seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39(2) the unpaid seller has a right of withholding delivery similar to and co-extensive with his rights of lien or retention and stoppage in transit` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller is an unpaid seller` AND (NOT `the property in the goods has passed to the buyer`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the right is given "Where the property in goods has not passed to the buyer" to "the unpaid seller". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `Unpaid seller's lien (ss 41 to 43)`

-- s 41(1).
-- src:1161 | 41.—(1) Subject to this Act, the unpaid seller of goods who is in
-- src:1162 | possession of them is entitled to retain possession of them until
-- src:1163 | payment or tender of the price in the following cases:
-- src:1165 | (a) where the goods have been sold without any stipulation as
-- src:1166 | to credit;
-- src:1168 | (b) where the goods have been sold on credit but the term of
-- src:1169 | credit has expired;
-- src:1171 | (c) where the buyer becomes insolvent.
@ref s 41(1) (src:1161-1171)
GIVEN `the seller is an unpaid seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller is in possession of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods have been sold without any stipulation as to credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods have been sold on credit but the term of credit has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer becomes insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41(1) the unpaid seller is entitled to retain possession of the goods until payment or tender of the price` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the seller is an unpaid seller`
         AND `the seller is in possession of the goods`
         AND (   `the goods have been sold without any stipulation as to credit`
              OR `the goods have been sold on credit but the term of credit has expired`
              OR `the buyer becomes insolvent`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the entitlement is given to "the unpaid seller of goods who is in possession of them" "in the following cases". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 41(2).
-- src:1173 | (2) The seller may exercise his lien or right of retention
-- src:1174 | notwithstanding that he is in possession of the goods as agent or
-- src:1175 | bailee or custodier for the buyer.
@ref s 41(2) (src:1173-1175)
GIVEN `the seller has a lien or right of retention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he is in possession of the goods as agent or bailee or custodier for the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 41(2) the seller may exercise his lien or right of retention although he is in possession as agent or bailee or custodier for the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller has a lien or right of retention` AND `he is in possession of the goods as agent or bailee or custodier for the buyer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the seller's "lien or right of retention" held "notwithstanding that he is in possession of the goods as agent or bailee or custodier for the buyer".
            NOTHING

-- s 42.
-- src:1179 | 42. Where an unpaid seller has made part delivery of the goods, he
-- src:1180 | may exercise his lien or right of retention on the remainder, unless
-- src:1181 | such part delivery has been made under such circumstances as to
-- src:1182 | show an agreement to waive the lien or right of retention.
@ref s 42 (src:1179-1182)
GIVEN `an unpaid seller has made part delivery of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part delivery was made under circumstances showing an agreement to waive the lien or right of retention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 42 the unpaid seller may exercise his lien or right of retention on the remainder` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an unpaid seller has made part delivery of the goods`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section applies "Where an unpaid seller has made part delivery of the goods". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the part delivery was made under circumstances showing an agreement to waive the lien or right of retention`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless such part delivery has been made under such circumstances as to show an agreement to waive the lien or right of retention"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "unless" is read as the text's no when the part delivery shows an agreement to waive.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 43(1).
-- src:1189 | 43.—(1) The unpaid seller of goods loses his lien or right of
-- src:1190 | retention in respect of them —
-- src:1192 | (a) when he delivers the goods to a carrier or other bailee or
-- src:1193 | custodier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer
-- src:1194 | without reserving the right of disposal of the goods;
-- src:1196 | (b) when the buyer or his agent lawfully obtains possession of
-- src:1197 | the goods;
-- src:1199 | (c) by waiver of the lien or right of retention.
@ref s 43(1) (src:1189-1199)
GIVEN `he delivers the goods to a carrier or other bailee or custodier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer without reserving the right of disposal of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer or his agent lawfully obtains possession of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the unpaid seller waives the lien or right of retention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 43(1) the unpaid seller loses his lien or right of retention` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `he delivers the goods to a carrier or other bailee or custodier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer without reserving the right of disposal of the goods`
          OR `the buyer or his agent lawfully obtains possession of the goods`
          OR `the unpaid seller waives the lien or right of retention`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names three occasions and does not say that the lien is retained on any other.
            NOTHING

-- s 43(2).
-- src:1201 | (2) An unpaid seller of goods who has a lien or right of retention in
-- src:1202 | respect of them does not lose his lien or right of retention by reason
-- src:1203 | only that he has obtained judgment or decree for the price of the
-- src:1204 | goods.
@ref s 43(2) (src:1201-1204)
GIVEN `the only thing that has happened is that he has obtained judgment or decree for the price of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 43(2) the unpaid seller loses his lien or right of retention by reason only of obtaining judgment or decree for the price` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the only thing that has happened is that he has obtained judgment or decree for the price of the goods`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not lose his lien or right of retention by reason only that he has obtained judgment or decree for the price of the goods"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a loss "by reason only" of a judgment or decree for the price.
            NOTHING

§§ `Stoppage in transit (ss 44 to 46)`

-- s 44, first limb: the right.
-- src:1210 | 44. Subject to this Act, when the buyer of goods becomes insolvent,
-- src:1211 | the unpaid seller who has parted with the possession of the goods has
-- src:1212 | the right of stopping them in transit, that is to say, he may resume
-- src:1213 | possession of the goods as long as they are in course of transit, and
-- src:1214 | may retain them until payment or tender of the price.
@ref s 44 right (src:1210-1214)
GIVEN `the buyer of goods becomes insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the unpaid seller has parted with the possession of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44 the unpaid seller has the right of stopping the goods in transit` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the buyer of goods becomes insolvent` AND `the unpaid seller has parted with the possession of the goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the right is given "when the buyer of goods becomes insolvent" to "the unpaid seller who has parted with the possession of the goods". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (w): "when" read as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05: "when" counts as "where"; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 44, second limb: while the goods are in transit.
-- src:1210 | 44. Subject to this Act, when the buyer of goods becomes insolvent,
-- src:1211 | the unpaid seller who has parted with the possession of the goods has
-- src:1212 | the right of stopping them in transit, that is to say, he may resume
-- src:1213 | possession of the goods as long as they are in course of transit, and
-- src:1214 | may retain them until payment or tender of the price.
@ref s 44 resume (src:1210-1214)
GIVEN `the unpaid seller has the right of stopping the goods in transit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are in course of transit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44 the unpaid seller may resume possession of the goods and retain them until payment or tender of the price` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the unpaid seller has the right of stopping the goods in transit`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): see the conditions of the right in s 44. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (f): follows the "implied" function: a condition or warranty that is not implied cannot be broken
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the goods are in course of transit`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he may resume possession of the goods as long as they are in course of transit"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "as long as" is read as the text's no once the goods are no longer in course of transit.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 45(1).
-- src:1218 | 45.—(1) Goods are deemed to be in course of transit from the time
-- src:1219 | when they are delivered to a carrier or other bailee or custodier for the
-- src:1220 | purpose of transmission to the buyer, until the buyer or his agent in
-- src:1221 | that behalf takes delivery of them from the carrier or other bailee or
-- src:1222 | custodier.
@ref s 45(1) (src:1218-1222)
GIVEN `the goods have been delivered to a carrier or other bailee or custodier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer or his agent in that behalf has taken delivery of them from the carrier or other bailee or custodier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 45(1) the goods are deemed to be in course of transit` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods have been delivered to a carrier or other bailee or custodier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer` AND (NOT `the buyer or his agent in that behalf has taken delivery of them from the carrier or other bailee or custodier`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the goods have been delivered to a carrier or other bailee or custodier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "from the time when they are delivered to a carrier or other bailee or custodier for the purpose of transmission to the buyer, until the buyer or his agent in that behalf takes delivery of them from the carrier"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "until" is read as the text's no once the buyer or his agent has taken delivery.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the deeming runs "from the time when they are delivered to a carrier or other bailee or custodier". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is no
            JUST FALSE

-- s 45(2).
-- src:1224 | (2) If the buyer or his agent in that behalf obtains delivery of the
-- src:1225 | goods before their arrival at the appointed destination, the transit is at
-- src:1226 | an end.
@ref s 45(2) (src:1224-1226)
GIVEN `the buyer or his agent in that behalf obtains delivery of the goods before their arrival at the appointed destination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 45(2) the transit is at an end` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the buyer or his agent in that behalf obtains delivery of the goods before their arrival at the appointed destination`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the buyer or his agent in that behalf obtains delivery of the goods before their arrival at the appointed destination, the transit is at an end" -- without that delivery this subsection does not end the transit. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 45(3).
-- src:1228 | (3) If, after the arrival of the goods at the appointed destination, the
-- src:1229 | carrier or other bailee or custodier acknowledges to the buyer or his
-- src:1230 | agent that he holds the goods on his behalf and continues in
-- src:1235 | possession of them as bailee or custodier for the buyer or his agent,
-- src:1236 | the transit is at an end, and it is immaterial that a further destination
-- src:1237 | for the goods may have been indicated by the buyer.
@ref s 45(3) (src:1228-1237)
GIVEN `the goods have arrived at the appointed destination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the carrier or other bailee or custodier acknowledges to the buyer or his agent that he holds the goods on his behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he continues in possession of them as bailee or custodier for the buyer or his agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 45(3) the transit is at an end` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods have arrived at the appointed destination` AND `the carrier or other bailee or custodier acknowledges to the buyer or his agent that he holds the goods on his behalf` AND `he continues in possession of them as bailee or custodier for the buyer or his agent`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "If, after the arrival of the goods at the appointed destination, the carrier or other bailee or custodier acknowledges ... and continues in possession". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 45(4).
-- src:1239 | (4) If the goods are rejected by the buyer, and the carrier or other
-- src:1240 | bailee or custodier continues in possession of them, the transit is not
-- src:1241 | deemed to be at an end, even if the seller has refused to receive them
-- src:1242 | back.
@ref s 45(4) (src:1239-1242)
GIVEN `the goods are rejected by the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the carrier or other bailee or custodier continues in possession of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 45(4) the transit is at an end` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods are rejected by the buyer` AND `the carrier or other bailee or custodier continues in possession of them`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the transit is not deemed to be at an end, even if the seller has refused to receive them back"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "If the goods are rejected by the buyer, and the carrier or other bailee or custodier continues in possession of them".
            NOTHING

-- s 45(5).
-- src:1244 | (5) When goods are delivered to a ship chartered by the buyer, it is a
-- src:1245 | question depending on the circumstances of the particular case
-- src:1246 | whether they are in the possession of the master as a carrier or as
-- src:1247 | agent to the buyer.
@ref s 45(5) (src:1244-1247)
GIVEN `the goods are delivered to a ship chartered by the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how the circumstances of the particular case answer the question` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 45(5) the goods are in the possession of the master as a carrier and not as agent to the buyer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the goods are delivered to a ship chartered by the buyer`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "When goods are delivered to a ship chartered by the buyer".
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "it is a question depending on the circumstances of the particular case"; a known answer is passed through, an unknown one is NOTHING.
            `how the circumstances of the particular case answer the question`

-- s 45(6).
-- src:1249 | (6) Where the carrier or other bailee or custodier wrongfully refuses
-- src:1250 | to deliver the goods to the buyer or his agent in that behalf, the transit
-- src:1251 | is deemed to be at an end.
@ref s 45(6) (src:1249-1251)
GIVEN `the carrier or other bailee or custodier wrongfully refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer or his agent in that behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 45(6) the transit is deemed to be at an end` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the carrier or other bailee or custodier wrongfully refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer or his agent in that behalf`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the carrier or other bailee or custodier wrongfully refuses to deliver the goods to the buyer or his agent in that behalf, the transit is deemed to be at an end" -- without that refusal this subsection does not end the transit. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 45(7).
-- src:1253 | (7) Where part delivery of the goods has been made to the buyer or
-- src:1254 | his agent in that behalf, the remainder of the goods may be stopped in
-- src:1255 | transit, unless such part delivery has been made under such
-- src:1256 | circumstances as to show an agreement to give up possession of
-- src:1257 | the whole of the goods.
@ref s 45(7) (src:1253-1257)
GIVEN `part delivery of the goods has been made to the buyer or his agent in that behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part delivery was made under circumstances showing an agreement to give up possession of the whole of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 45(7) the remainder of the goods may be stopped in transit` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `part delivery of the goods has been made to the buyer or his agent in that behalf`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where part delivery of the goods has been made to the buyer or his agent in that behalf". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the part delivery was made under circumstances showing an agreement to give up possession of the whole of the goods`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless such part delivery has been made under such circumstances as to show an agreement to give up possession of the whole of the goods"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "unless" is read as the text's no when the part delivery shows an agreement to give up possession of the whole.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ss 45(1) to (7) gathered by hand (E1 option B): whether the goods are in course of transit.
-- Each subsection's own function above gives its own answer (option C); this one only combines them.
-- src:1218 | 45.—(1) Goods are deemed to be in course of transit from the time
-- src:1219 | when they are delivered to a carrier or other bailee or custodier for the
-- src:1220 | purpose of transmission to the buyer, until the buyer or his agent in
-- src:1221 | that behalf takes delivery of them from the carrier or other bailee or
-- src:1222 | custodier.
-- src:1224 | (2) If the buyer or his agent in that behalf obtains delivery of the
-- src:1225 | goods before their arrival at the appointed destination, the transit is at
-- src:1226 | an end.
-- src:1228 | (3) If, after the arrival of the goods at the appointed destination, the
-- src:1229 | carrier or other bailee or custodier acknowledges to the buyer or his
-- src:1230 | agent that he holds the goods on his behalf and continues in
-- src:1235 | possession of them as bailee or custodier for the buyer or his agent,
-- src:1236 | the transit is at an end, and it is immaterial that a further destination
-- src:1237 | for the goods may have been indicated by the buyer.
-- src:1239 | (4) If the goods are rejected by the buyer, and the carrier or other
-- src:1240 | bailee or custodier continues in possession of them, the transit is not
-- src:1241 | deemed to be at an end, even if the seller has refused to receive them
-- src:1242 | back.
-- src:1244 | (5) When goods are delivered to a ship chartered by the buyer, it is a
-- src:1245 | question depending on the circumstances of the particular case
-- src:1246 | whether they are in the possession of the master as a carrier or as
-- src:1247 | agent to the buyer.
-- src:1249 | (6) Where the carrier or other bailee or custodier wrongfully refuses
-- src:1250 | to deliver the goods to the buyer or his agent in that behalf, the transit
-- src:1251 | is deemed to be at an end.
-- src:1253 | (7) Where part delivery of the goods has been made to the buyer or
-- src:1254 | his agent in that behalf, the remainder of the goods may be stopped in
-- src:1255 | transit, unless such part delivery has been made under such
-- src:1256 | circumstances as to show an agreement to give up possession of
-- src:1257 | the whole of the goods.
@ref ss 45(1) to (7) (src:1218-1257)
GIVEN `s 45(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 45(2) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 45(3) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 45(4) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 45(6) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 45(1) to (7) the goods are in course of transit` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 45(4) answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN
            -- s 45(4): "the transit is not deemed to be at an end" -- so the goods are still in transit (a yes to this question, from the text's no to "at an end").
            JUST TRUE
        IF `s 45(2) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 45(3) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 45(6) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the transit is at an end" (s 45(2), (3)) or "the transit is deemed to be at an end" (s 45(6)).
            JUST FALSE
        IF `s 45(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 45(1) answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 45(1) deems goods in transit only from delivery to a carrier or other bailee or custodier.
            NOTHING

-- s 46(1).
-- src:1261 | 46.—(1) The unpaid seller may exercise his right of stoppage in
-- src:1262 | transit either by taking actual possession of the goods or by giving
-- src:1263 | notice of his claim to the carrier or other bailee or custodier in whose
-- src:1264 | possession the goods are.
