GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46(1) the unpaid seller may exercise his right of stoppage in transit by this method` IS
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `taking actual possession of the goods` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `giving notice of his claim to the carrier or other bailee or custodier in whose possession the goods are` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection says the right may be exercised "either" way and does not say that no other method is allowed.
    WHEN `some other method` THEN NOTHING

-- s 46(2).
