        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If given to the principal, the notice is ineffective unless given at such time and under such circumstances that the principal, by the exercise of reasonable diligence, may communicate it to his servant or agent in time to prevent a delivery to the buyer."
            -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "unless" is read as the text's no; the other reading is that "unless" states an exception only and the text is silent when it fails.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when a notice to the principal is ineffective; it does not say that a timely notice is effective.
            NOTHING

