§§ `Re-sale, etc., by buyer (s 47) and rescission and re-sale by seller (s 48)`

-- s 47(1).
-- src:1286 | 47.—(1) Subject to this Act, the unpaid seller’s right of lien or
-- src:1287 | retention or stoppage in transit is not affected by any sale or other
-- src:1288 | disposition of the goods which the buyer may have made, unless the
-- src:1289 | seller has assented to it.
@ref s 47(1) (src:1286-1289)
GIVEN `the buyer has made a sale or other disposition of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller has assented to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 47(1) the unpaid seller's right of lien or retention or stoppage in transit is affected by the buyer's sale or other disposition` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the buyer has made a sale or other disposition of the goods`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "any sale or other disposition of the goods which the buyer may have made".
            NOTHING
        IF `the seller has assented to it`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the seller has assented to it" -- the subsection then says nothing about the effect.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the unpaid seller’s right of lien or retention or stoppage in transit is not affected by any sale or other disposition of the goods which the buyer may have made"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 47(2)(a), (b).
-- src:1291 | (2) Where a document of title to goods has been lawfully
-- src:1292 | transferred to any person as buyer or owner of the goods, and that
-- src:1293 | person transfers the document to a person who takes it in good faith
-- src:1294 | and for valuable consideration, then —
-- src:1296 | (a) if the last-mentioned transfer was by way of sale, the
-- src:1297 | unpaid seller’s right of lien or retention or stoppage in
-- src:1298 | transit is defeated; and
-- src:1300 | (b) if the last-mentioned transfer was made by way of pledge
-- src:1301 | or other disposition for value, the unpaid seller’s right of
-- src:1302 | lien or retention or stoppage in transit can only be
-- src:1303 | exercised subject to the rights of the transferee.
@ref s 47(2) (src:1291-1303)
GIVEN `a document of title to goods has been lawfully transferred to a person as buyer or owner of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person transfers the document to a person who takes it in good faith and for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer to that person` IS A `Disposition of a document of title by the buyer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 47(2) the unpaid seller's right of lien or retention or stoppage in transit is defeated` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a document of title to goods has been lawfully transferred to a person as buyer or owner of the goods` AND `that person transfers the document to a person who takes it in good faith and for valuable consideration`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where a document of title to goods has been lawfully transferred to any person as buyer or owner of the goods, and that person transfers the document to a person who takes it in good faith and for valuable consideration". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the transfer to that person` EQUALS `a sale by the transferee`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the transfer to that person` EQUALS `a pledge or other disposition for value`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the last-mentioned transfer was made by way of pledge or other disposition for value, the unpaid seller’s right of lien or retention or stoppage in transit can only be exercised subject to the rights of the transferee" -- the right is not defeated; it is subject to the transferee's rights.
            -- MARGINAL (a): a failed "can only be exercised subject to" is read as the text's no; the other reading is that "can only be exercised subject to" states an exception only and the text is silent when it fails.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection deals with a transfer by way of sale and one by way of pledge or other disposition for value.
            NOTHING

-- s 47(2)(b).
-- src:1291 | (2) Where a document of title to goods has been lawfully
-- src:1292 | transferred to any person as buyer or owner of the goods, and that
-- src:1293 | person transfers the document to a person who takes it in good faith
